%% One refund request through all five stacks. X-Trace-Id and X-User-Id travel on every hop.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer (client)
    participant R as router (OpenAI Agents SDK)
    participant L as LLM gateway
    participant P as policy (LangGraph)
    participant K as risk (CrewAI)
    participant F as refund (Google ADK)
    participant N as notify (AutoGen)

    C->>R: POST /tasks "refund ORD-1001"
    R->>R: load SQLiteSession(context_id) + user case file
    R->>L: chat (history + tools)
    L-->>R: tool_call ask_policy

    R->>P: POST /tasks (question)
    P->>P: recall long-term store, checkpoint
    P->>L: chat (+ search_policy tool)
    L-->>P: tool_call search_policy
    P-->>R: policy text

    R->>L: chat (+ policy result)
    L-->>R: tool_call ask_risk
    R->>K: POST /tasks (order, amount, customer)
    K->>L: chat (+ assess_risk tool)
    K-->>R: {score, decision}

    alt decision == approve
        R->>F: POST /tasks "refund ORD-1001 $120"
        F->>F: issue_refund, write user:/app: state + ledger
        F-->>R: refunded
    else decision == escalate
        Note over R,F: refund agent is never called
    end

    R->>N: POST /tasks "tell the customer"
    N->>N: send_email to outbox, append ListMemory, save_state
    N-->>R: queued

    R->>R: append case-file note
    R-->>C: final answer + nested tool_calls
